Hi all,

I am encountering a couple of errors running the procD.lm and advanced.procD.lm functions, to look at the effect of habitat (flowing/non-flowing - 2 levels), location (river or reservoir where fish are sampled - 11 locations) and sex (3 levels - m, f, immature) on body shape.

Using procD.lm, I have specified the following models and received the following output from R:

y~habitat*sex # no problem here, summary output is given. Same for location*sex.
y~habitat*location*sex # Error in data.frame(df, SS, MS, Rsq = R2, F = Fs) : arguments imply differing number of rows: 9, 7

I'll hazard a guess and say, that the error from the second formula is due to a deg of freedom problem? I'm not sure if that is a problem when using multiple interactions in an ANOVA framework, since there are 3 two-way and 1 three-way interactions for the second formula.
I do have different levels for each factor (i.e. for location, I have 5 reservoirs and 6 rivers; for sex, I have male, female and immature and for some locations, there are only 3-5 males, so that is why I though df or sample size might be a problem).

The other errors occurring using advanced.procD.lm are as follows.

When specifying

 smelt.shp4<-advanced.procD.lm(smeltshp.gpa$coords~habitat2*sex2, ~habitat2+sex2, groups=habitat2*sex2, iter=99)

I get the following error

 Error in advanced.procD.lm(smeltshp.gpa$coords ~ habitat2 * sex2, ~habitat2 +  :
  Models have same df

So I tried this:
> smelt.shp4<-advanced.procD.lm(smeltshp.gpa$coords~habitat2*sex2, ~habitat2+sex2, iter=99)

But I get the same error:

Error in advanced.procD.lm(smeltshp.gpa$coords ~ habitat2 * sex2, ~habitat2 +  :
  Models have same df

Lastly, I tried the following:
> smelt.shp4<-advanced.procD.lm(smeltshp.gpa$coords~habitat2+sex2, ~habitat2*sex2*location2, iter=99)

But to no avail:
Error in advanced.procD.lm(smeltshp.gpa$coords ~ habitat2 + sex2, ~habitat2 * : Models have same df

And one more:
> smelt.shp4<-advanced.procD.lm(smeltshp.gpa$coords~habitat2+location2+sex2, ~location2*sex2, iter=99)
Error in advanced.procD.lm(smeltshp.gpa$coords ~ habitat2 + location2 +  :
  Models have same df

I have read the R documentation for the function, and tried to follow the model structures in the examples. I also tried including the "groups"  argument, containing the respective interaction of the above models with the same result.

I'm not sure though, if what I'm trying to achieve will work with those structures and the data I have. My variables, in reality, are nested as follows: sex within location, within habitat. So if I am primarily interested in what shape differences are between habitats and locations, and if the differences (which I know exist from running procD.lm) are attributable to particular habitat/sex and location/sex combinations, how would I specify my model formulae?

I'm not clear on what the 'groups' argument is for, and whether or not I need it, and how it should be specified. I suspect if I am interested in interactions, that I should be seeking to use the slope comparisons, correct?

Ultimately, I would like to summarize the pairwise differences (habitat*sex) and (location*sex) as pairwise Euclidean distances or a comparable metric (similar to Collyer, Sekora & Adams, 2015), as this seems to be the most commonly reported way of doing this for Procrustes ANOVA. I am probably not aware of all them, so I am open to alternatives if there are other ways of summarizing pairwise differences and if these are accessible in geomorph or other R packages.

Alternatively, is there a way to quantify the pairwise differences of habitat*sex and location*sex based on the models using procD.lm? That function seems to be working, but generating pairwise differences seem to be accessible only in advanced.procD.lm.

Any help is greatly appreciated.

Regards,

Daniel.

